Wed May 10 09:01:08 PDT 1989

This version of mstats does not yet support the -c and -r options, BUT:

-- it is much less sensitive to roundoff error.  All floating-point arithmetic
   is done in double precision.  In one memorable case, the old mstats
   reported a NEGATIVE variance for a an image with a small absolute range of
   values.

-- it's twice as fast as the old one (on Sun-3's, anyway ...)

Please try this mstats on any test cases you have and report the results to
frew@crseo.ucsb.edu.  Thanks.

